        // usually a bend — the ramp arrives at exactly that minute — so a
        // tick there lay over the corner: on a vertical drop it read as the
        // line overshooting its own rail, on a 45° ramp as a blot. A dot
        // sits ON the line instead of across it, so it reads as a mark on
